<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso XIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1886">1886</a>–<a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Alfonso XIII of Spain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso XIII was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from his birth in 1886 until 1931. His reign followed the loss of the last colonies in 1898 and saw the costly war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and the disaster at Annual in 1921, and growing labour unrest. He accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-primo-de-rivera">Miguel Primo de Rivera</a>'s dictatorship in 1923, which discredited the monarchy. After republicans won the municipal elections of April 1931 he left Spain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-xiii.jpg" alt="Alfonso XIII" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaulak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rey_Alfonso_XIII_de_Espa%C3%B1a,_by_Kaulak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
